# Pairs with RestoredCutNotReAdvanced. The cutover pauses shipping but not
# receiving, so a laggard cluster that has not cut over yet ships a
# pre-restore write straight into an early cluster's restored copy - the
# re-advance the receive fence exists to stop.
MODULE: RestoredCutNotReAdvancedCommitLeavesReceiveOpen
TARGET: RestoredCutNotReAdvanced
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the commit fence does not pause inbound apply
PERTURBS: Commit

--- FIND
    /\ recvOn' = [recvOn EXCEPT ![c] = FALSE]
--- REPLACE
    \* MUTATION: receive stays open.
    /\ UNCHANGED recvOn
--- END
